{
  "purpose": "Confound check: does NB beat Poisson under scVI gene-cell amortized dispersion because of theta's CELL-CONDITIONALITY, or merely because that arm's mean is worse (deeper variance deficit)? mu is IDENTICAL in all three arms, so a mean deficit cannot confound this contrast.",
  "deviation_from_literal_request": "sample_nb_fixed_theta only accepts a scalar/inf theta; theta_g is a PER-GENE vector (median over cells of the amortized theta_ic), so (ii) nb_global_theta was drawn with sample_nb(mu, theta_g_broadcast) instead -- the identical Gamma-Poisson mixture, just via the array-capable function. See module docstring.",
  "no_retraining_caveat": "scVI gene-cell was NOT checkpointed in the main run (only aggregate metrics were persisted), so extracting raw mu_ic/theta_ic required one re-fit at the SAME seed/config already used -- not a new model or hyperparameter change. See module docstring.",
